file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived_confi
    > dential/95%-sample/h1_dataset.dta saved

. 
. 
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.  
. * Example: only keep participants from private households
. keep if inlist(pop,1,2)
(89,279 observations deleted)

. 
. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES * 
. 
. * Example: generate dummy variable for whether participant has at least one d
> aughter (1) or not (0)
. * Create treatment: has at least one daughter
. gen has_daughter = 0

. replace has_daughter = 1 if inlist(kidsex01, 2) | inlist(kidsex02, 2) | ///
>                          inlist(kidsex03, 2) | inlist(kidsex04, 2) | ///
>                          inlist(kidsex05, 2)
(277,754 real changes made)

. 
. * Generate some control variables
. gen male = (sex == 1)

. gen age = bioage

. gen income = hghinc 

. gen num_kids = sumkids 

. gen educ = pgbilzeit  
(62,122 missing values generated)

. replace educ = . if pgbilzeit < 0
(27,693 real changes made, 27,693 to missing)

. gen region = birthregion if birthregion > 0
(302,978 missing values generated)

. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * 
. 
. *We originally intended to use attitudinal variables like bjp166_02, but this
>  is wave-specific and not in our merged dataset.
. 
. * So we are reframing H1 (Behavioral Proxy)
. *New H1 (Behavioral): "Having daughters is associated with greater involvemen
> t in domestic tasks, as measured by daily time spent on housework."
. *This serves as a behavioral proxy for gender-role attitudes: individuals who
>  spend more time on housework may hold more egalitarian views, especially if 
> male.
. 
. gen gender_eq_attitude = pli0043_h
(67,373 missing values generated)

. replace gender_eq_attitude = . if gender_eq_attitude < 0
(18,819 real changes made, 18,819 to missing)

. 
. reg gender_eq_attitude has_daughter male age educ income num_kids i.region i.
> syear, r

